{
  "name": "18-refuse-frozen-constitutional-collision",
  "description": "The hole in the safety argument. The decision record claims frozen 'cannot widen agent authority' because issuing one renounces amendment power. That holds ONLY if a frozen policy cannot govern a constitutional field. Here an agent mints class=frozen on capital.max_at_risk with value 100,000,000, colliding with Evan's constitutional ceiling of 5,000 -- a ceiling it granted ITSELF which, by construction, NOBODY INCLUDING THE PRINCIPAL may ever amend. The self-authorization firewall breached by the very class claimed incapable of breaching it, and made irreversible. Refused by rule 17 at Policy-emission time; no Decision is needed for the violation to exist.",
